lisa-design:
- Files come from catalog.Assets of the live snapshot only (Prompts.Text/Digest, SchemaSources); no disk reads, so the path check is a contract rule, not the only guard against traversal.
- Path rule: path.Clean(p) == p, no backslash, under prompts/ or schemas/ with a name, at most 512 bytes; anything else is 400 invalid, a valid path the snapshot lacks is 404. The list applies the same rule, so it never lists a file get would refuse.
- A schema's digest is sha256 of its raw bytes (the catalog stores none for schemas); a prompt's is the catalog's own Prompt.Digest.

